# The declaring module, with an `extern` the header refuses.
#
# `math.h` declares `double sqrt(double)`. This says `i64` both ways, so
# clang's own check on the probe block rejects it, and the diagnostic
# lands HERE — on the author's line, in the module that declared it —
# rather than in whatever translation unit happened to be compiling.
#
# The wrapper exists because acceptance row 1 forbids reaching an
# `extern` across a module boundary: the caller reaches `root`, and only
# this module carries the header.

extern "math.h" link "m"
    function sqrt(x: i64) -> i64                    #~ ffi_return_type

function root(x: i64) -> i64
    return sqrt(x: x)
